FlowUp keeps one canonical rule set; this file is a pointer only.

Read before writing code, in order:
1. AGENTS.md (repository rules, authoritative)
2. AGENT_ADAPTER.md (rule loading, document resolution, task loop, reporting)
3. apps/api/AGENTS.md for backend work, apps/web/AGENTS.md for frontend work
4. The task row in docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, or that task's specification in docs/phase-1/ (BE-XX.md / FE-XX.md)

Approved documents in docs/ are the source of truth. Report document conflicts instead of resolving them silently. Use the final report format in AGENT_ADAPTER.md section 7.
